1
00:00:03,440 --> 00:00:03,960
Chengcheng,

2
00:00:04,240 --> 00:00:06,360
give Churan a little test.

3
00:00:06,640 --> 00:00:09,760
Since she listed singing and dancing as talents,

4
00:00:09,760 --> 00:00:11,480
pick either singing or dancing.

5
00:00:12,560 --> 00:00:13,360
Well,

6
00:00:14,080 --> 00:00:15,040
that's a bit beyond the syllabus.

7
00:00:17,440 --> 00:00:18,360
What do you think?

8
00:00:18,360 --> 00:00:19,560
Sure, I can do it.

9
00:00:19,560 --> 00:00:20,560
Right now is fine, right?

10
00:00:20,560 --> 00:00:21,360
Sure.

11
00:00:24,760 --> 00:00:25,640
I don't know how.

12
00:00:25,640 --> 00:00:27,400
Why don't you do one with the team leader?

13
00:00:29,280 --> 00:00:30,080
That works too.

14
00:00:30,400 --> 00:00:30,880
Let's do it.

15
00:00:30,880 --> 00:00:31,680
Come on.

16
00:00:33,240 --> 00:00:35,200
Feels like the team leader doesn't need me to teach him.

17
00:00:37,000 --> 00:00:38,160
He's already got into the groove.

18
00:00:48,600 --> 00:00:49,640
Hit the music!

19
00:01:02,560 --> 00:01:03,920
Nice, not bad.

20
00:01:03,920 --> 00:01:04,880
He definitely has the moves.

21
00:01:08,760 --> 00:01:09,720
Shen Teng can't get old.

22
00:01:09,720 --> 00:01:10,640
If he gets any older, he'll definitely be...

23
00:01:10,640 --> 00:01:12,120
...a total killer at square dancing.

24
00:01:15,240 --> 00:01:16,440
Not bad.

25
00:01:17,080 --> 00:01:18,120
So did we pass?

26
00:01:18,120 --> 00:01:18,920
Passed!

27
00:01:25,880 --> 00:01:26,480
Five characters!

28
00:01:26,920 --> 00:01:27,440
Who is he?

29
00:01:27,680 --> 00:01:28,160
Shen Teng!

30
00:01:29,560 --> 00:01:29,960
Eat!

31
00:01:35,040 --> 00:01:35,440
Eat!

32
00:01:37,280 --> 00:01:37,640
Eat!

33
00:01:39,920 --> 00:01:40,880
Shen Teng eats...

34
00:01:42,520 --> 00:01:43,480
Shen Teng eats...

35
00:01:46,040 --> 00:01:46,720
The third character.

36
00:01:49,240 --> 00:01:49,720
Eat!

37
00:01:51,640 --> 00:01:52,760
Shen Teng eats...

38
00:01:56,280 --> 00:01:56,920
Five characters!

39
00:01:57,360 --> 00:01:59,120
What's the fourth character?

40
00:01:59,520 --> 00:02:00,400
The fourth character!

41
00:02:04,680 --> 00:02:05,440
The last two characters!

42
00:02:06,040 --> 00:02:06,840
What am I doing?

43
00:02:10,760 --> 00:02:12,120
Shen Teng loves soybean paste!

44
00:02:12,960 --> 00:02:13,880
This is the fourth character!

45
00:02:13,880 --> 00:02:14,960
This is just the fourth character!

46
00:02:21,400 --> 00:02:23,720
Shen Teng loves steamed buns!

47
00:02:26,200 --> 00:02:26,960
Grind!

48
00:02:27,920 --> 00:02:28,400
Grind!

49
00:02:33,760 --> 00:02:34,440
The fifth character!

50
00:02:36,080 --> 00:02:38,920
Shen Teng eats buns!

51
00:02:43,960 --> 00:02:45,440
Shen Teng and Anyu are both very suspicious.

52
00:02:45,440 --> 00:02:46,280
They played well.

53
00:02:51,240 --> 00:02:52,440
You couldn't even guess that?

54
00:02:52,440 --> 00:02:53,840
Shen Teng loves buns!

55
00:02:53,840 --> 00:02:54,760
Where did "loves" come from?

56
00:02:55,400 --> 00:02:55,960
Five characters!

57
00:02:59,160 --> 00:02:59,800
Donkey!

58
00:03:00,520 --> 00:03:01,120
Mo!

59
00:03:02,640 --> 00:03:03,280
Shen Teng!

60
00:03:03,920 --> 00:03:04,680
Shen Teng!

61
00:03:05,280 --> 00:03:06,240
Bun donkey!

62
00:03:07,320 --> 00:03:09,200
Shen Teng loves what bun donkey?

63
00:03:13,880 --> 00:03:14,760
Still haven't guessed it?

64
00:03:18,760 --> 00:03:20,320
Loves bun donkey, Shen Teng eats...

65
00:03:24,280 --> 00:03:24,920
Eats a donkey?

66
00:03:27,880 --> 00:03:29,000
I know Shen Teng!

67
00:03:29,000 --> 00:03:30,400
Grind! Eat!

68
00:03:30,400 --> 00:03:31,040
What else?

69
00:03:31,040 --> 00:03:32,360
Make a word! Put it together!

70
00:03:32,920 --> 00:03:33,920
Just two characters left!

71
00:03:38,200 --> 00:03:38,520
Thick!

72
00:03:39,120 --> 00:03:39,440
Face!

73
00:03:39,600 --> 00:03:40,320
Eat face?

74
00:03:41,760 --> 00:03:42,560
What's this?

75
00:03:44,680 --> 00:03:46,320
What on earth is that? Growing on the ground!

76
00:03:49,080 --> 00:03:50,640
You couldn't guess this, Chengcheng?

77
00:03:54,080 --> 00:03:56,520
You even guessed "mo"!

78
00:03:57,720 --> 00:03:58,960
Shen Teng eats mushrooms!

79
00:04:02,560 --> 00:04:04,640
What's wrong with you?

80
00:04:05,120 --> 00:04:06,320
You didn't guess that?

81
00:04:11,440 --> 00:04:12,360
What are you making?

82
00:04:12,560 --> 00:04:14,000
Chili peppers with soybean paste.

83
00:04:17,040 --> 00:04:17,960
Gongjin Fried Eggs.

84
00:04:19,000 --> 00:04:19,960
What fried eggs?

85
00:04:19,960 --> 00:04:21,160
Have you ever heard of Gongjin Fried Eggs?

86
00:04:21,160 --> 00:04:21,880
What's that?

87
00:04:21,880 --> 00:04:22,840
Gongjin Fried Eggs.

88
00:04:23,800 --> 00:04:25,080
Did I mishear you?

89
00:04:25,080 --> 00:04:27,000
Never heard of this dish before, have you?

90
00:04:27,000 --> 00:04:27,800
It's delicious.

91
00:04:28,440 --> 00:04:30,200
Did you wash that chili pepper?

92
00:04:30,200 --> 00:04:31,000
Yeah, I washed it.

93
00:04:32,600 --> 00:04:34,120
Bell peppers are better.

94
00:04:34,800 --> 00:04:37,040
Bell peppers are the most nutritious.

95
00:04:37,920 --> 00:04:39,040
Gongjin Fried Eggs.

96
00:04:39,040 --> 00:04:40,080
What's "Gongjin"?

97
00:04:40,080 --> 00:04:41,360
The name of the dish.

98
00:04:41,360 --> 00:04:42,320
Gongsun Li?

99
00:04:43,280 --> 00:04:44,480
I'm suddenly getting hungry.

100
00:04:46,160 --> 00:04:47,440
I'm calling it a day.

101
00:04:47,440 --> 00:04:48,240
Not cooking anymore.

102
00:04:48,240 --> 00:04:49,280
If you want some, I can make it.

103
00:04:49,640 --> 00:04:50,440
Just take a break.

104
00:04:55,960 --> 00:04:57,440
I've already chewed through a whole pepper.

105
00:04:57,440 --> 00:04:59,040
Can't you see how starving I am?

106
00:05:02,280 --> 00:05:03,200
It's super nutritious.

107
00:05:04,160 --> 00:05:04,960
Full of vitamins.

108
00:05:09,800 --> 00:05:12,000
Want some? I broke off a piece.

109
00:05:20,880 --> 00:05:21,840
Here comes a wave!

110
00:05:24,760 --> 00:05:26,240
This actually looks pretty cool.

111
00:05:30,200 --> 00:05:31,640
Show me the biggest one, will you?

112
00:05:31,640 --> 00:05:32,640
The one just now was the biggest.

113
00:05:32,640 --> 00:05:33,440
Give me the wildest wave!

114
00:05:33,440 --> 00:05:34,240
That one's three meters high!

115
00:05:35,000 --> 00:05:37,280
No, when you're out there riding it,

116
00:05:37,280 --> 00:05:38,400
you get tossed up three meters!

117
00:05:38,680 --> 00:05:40,680
Not that the wave itself is three meters.

118
00:05:41,920 --> 00:05:43,120
Come on, give it a shot.

119
00:05:43,800 --> 00:05:44,600
Let's do it!

120
00:05:49,800 --> 00:05:50,760
He charged right in! Let's go!

121
00:05:51,720 --> 00:05:52,680
Do you know how to do this?

122
00:05:53,480 --> 00:05:54,560
The instructor isn't even here yet.

123
00:05:54,720 --> 00:05:55,560
He doesn't need an instructor.

124
00:05:55,560 --> 00:05:57,000
Go on, get over there, hurry!

125
00:05:57,360 --> 00:05:58,800
Does Johnny Huang need an instructor?

126
00:05:59,440 --> 00:06:00,760
Being here is like coming home to him.

127
00:06:00,760 --> 00:06:01,080
Alright.

128
00:06:01,080 --> 00:06:02,360
Students!

129
00:06:02,360 --> 00:06:04,200
It's dangerous, come back right now!

130
00:06:06,760 --> 00:06:07,480
Come back, come back!

131
00:06:08,120 --> 00:06:10,040
He just tossed his board right in!

132
00:06:13,320 --> 00:06:14,160
Does a mimosa...

133
00:06:14,160 --> 00:06:16,160
have faster reactions, or does a human?

134
00:06:18,400 --> 00:06:19,200
A mimosa.

135
00:06:21,600 --> 00:06:23,640
Good thing I reacted a bit faster than a mimosa.

136
00:06:25,960 --> 00:06:28,400
A mimosa has a reaction time of just 0.1 seconds,

137
00:06:28,400 --> 00:06:30,520
while a human's is 0.2 seconds.

138
00:06:51,280 --> 00:06:53,120
No need for a solo camera on Dr. Chen for this part.

139
00:06:55,760 --> 00:06:58,320
There's even a dedicated camera for him.

140
00:06:58,320 --> 00:06:59,360
I'll make sure you get a vertical shot.

141
00:06:59,360 --> 00:07:01,760
Dr. Chen's express tutorial!

142
00:07:07,920 --> 00:07:10,040
Stand up and turn your body.

143
00:07:11,080 --> 00:07:12,480
Wait, that's not right.

144
00:07:13,440 --> 00:07:15,400
Why am I facing everyone?

145
00:07:16,600 --> 00:07:18,560
So how do we classify the stances?

146
00:07:18,560 --> 00:07:20,240
Regular and Goofy.

147
00:07:20,240 --> 00:07:22,640
Left foot forward is the regular stance.

148
00:07:22,640 --> 00:07:24,800
Right foot forward is the goofy stance.

149
00:07:24,800 --> 00:07:26,720
Then all of you are goofy.

150
00:07:26,960 --> 00:07:28,200
I'm naturally left-handed.

151
00:07:28,680 --> 00:07:29,800
I'm a lefty too!

152
00:07:29,800 --> 00:07:31,040
Then you're just standing wrong.

153
00:07:31,040 --> 00:07:31,840
Fair enough.

154
00:07:33,040 --> 00:07:34,240
Just go with whatever feels natural.

155
00:07:34,240 --> 00:07:35,720
Whatever helps you stand up on instinct.

156
00:07:35,720 --> 00:07:37,040
Right, do whatever works for you.

157
00:07:37,760 --> 00:07:39,360
So how do we get off the board?

158
00:07:39,360 --> 00:07:40,680
There are two ways.

159
00:07:40,680 --> 00:07:41,800
First, steady your balance.

160
00:07:41,800 --> 00:07:42,840
Crouch down onto the board.

161
00:07:42,840 --> 00:07:44,160
Hold onto the deck.

162
00:07:44,160 --> 00:07:46,040
Push off and step down from the side.

163
00:07:48,000 --> 00:07:50,120
The second way is falling off.

164
00:07:50,360 --> 00:07:52,560
The moment you hit the water, protect your head.

165
00:07:52,840 --> 00:07:54,600
Right, protect your head.

166
00:07:55,920 --> 00:07:57,160
When you take an unplanned plunge,

167
00:07:57,160 --> 00:07:58,160
after you fall in,

168
00:07:58,160 --> 00:07:59,480
aren't you separated from the board?

169
00:07:59,480 --> 00:08:00,240
Right.

170
00:08:00,240 --> 00:08:01,440
What should you look for then?

171
00:08:01,440 --> 00:08:02,400
It's this right here.

172
00:08:03,280 --> 00:08:03,840
The cord.

173
00:08:03,840 --> 00:08:04,720
Look for your ankle leash.

174
00:08:05,240 --> 00:08:06,840
This leash is also known as our...

175
00:08:06,840 --> 00:08:07,880
"Lifeline."

176
00:08:07,880 --> 00:08:09,880
The safety leash is absolutely crucial.

177
00:08:10,080 --> 00:08:11,120
It has two ends.

178
00:08:11,120 --> 00:08:13,280
The small end attaches to the board.

179
00:08:13,280 --> 00:08:14,920
The large end straps around your leg.

180
00:08:14,920 --> 00:08:16,920
The coach already attached the small end for you.

181
00:08:17,040 --> 00:08:18,720
Let's see how to strap the large end.

182
00:08:18,920 --> 00:08:20,000
It's Velcro.

183
00:08:21,200 --> 00:08:22,360
Just pull it tight and stick it.

184
00:08:25,160 --> 00:08:26,200
Right, perfect.

185
00:08:34,760 --> 00:08:35,720
You go first.

186
00:08:47,600 --> 00:08:48,680
Hold on.

187
00:08:48,680 --> 00:08:50,400
Wait, no.

188
00:08:50,400 --> 00:08:51,560
Hey, no stalling!

189
00:08:53,760 --> 00:08:54,960
I almost lost.

190
00:08:56,400 --> 00:08:58,080
She's attacking from both sides.

191
00:08:59,200 --> 00:09:01,040
She's got great game sense.

192
00:09:01,400 --> 00:09:03,600
She looks so relaxed, while you look...

193
00:09:04,160 --> 00:09:05,120
a bit too stressed.

194
00:09:05,120 --> 00:09:06,040
I can't beat her.

195
00:09:06,640 --> 00:09:07,520
It is what it is.

196
00:09:07,960 --> 00:09:09,760
Don't tell me she's actually a genius?

197
00:09:12,280 --> 00:09:13,040
I won, right?

198
00:09:13,360 --> 00:09:14,160
You won.

199
00:09:14,600 --> 00:09:15,360
How did you win?

200
00:09:15,360 --> 00:09:16,480
How'd you pull that off?

201
00:09:16,480 --> 00:09:16,960
I couldn't even follow it.

202
00:09:16,960 --> 00:09:18,960
She won, right here.

203
00:09:19,920 --> 00:09:20,720
How come?

204
00:09:21,560 --> 00:09:23,720
Look, if he plays here, that's four in a row.

205
00:09:24,200 --> 00:09:26,000
And if he plays here, that's four too.

206
00:09:28,400 --> 00:09:30,760
Look at him, can't even follow the game.

207
00:09:31,440 --> 00:09:32,000
Let me try.

208
00:09:32,000 --> 00:09:32,640
You're up.

209
00:09:32,920 --> 00:09:33,720
You go first.

210
00:09:34,000 --> 00:09:34,800
All right.

211
00:09:36,120 --> 00:09:38,000
Churan, did you take classes as a kid?

212
00:09:38,000 --> 00:09:38,440
In Gomoku?

213
00:09:38,720 --> 00:09:40,240
I took Go classes.

214
00:09:40,440 --> 00:09:40,960
See?

215
00:09:42,040 --> 00:09:43,520
Then you should play Go with Xiao Hu.

216
00:09:43,520 --> 00:09:44,720
Xiao Hu is pretty good at Go too.

217
00:09:45,160 --> 00:09:45,840
Really?

218
00:09:47,640 --> 00:09:49,120
Then Chengcheng is about to win!

219
00:09:49,560 --> 00:09:50,680
I didn't even notice.

220
00:09:51,080 --> 00:09:51,760
He's going to win.

221
00:09:51,880 --> 00:09:52,320
Not yet.

222
00:09:52,320 --> 00:09:53,600
Feels like it's close.

223
00:09:53,840 --> 00:09:55,040
Just a move or two away.

224
00:09:55,720 --> 00:09:57,600
Just make a four right now.

225
00:09:57,600 --> 00:09:59,000
Got it, Cheng?

226
00:10:03,560 --> 00:10:04,440
Keep at it!

227
00:10:08,240 --> 00:10:10,280
He won! It's already in the bag!

228
00:10:10,800 --> 00:10:11,600
Won what?

229
00:10:12,880 --> 00:10:14,560
Let's see where he puts this one.

230
00:10:15,160 --> 00:10:16,480
Wherever he puts it, he can't win.

231
00:10:16,480 --> 00:10:17,840
If he puts it there, he wins!

232
00:10:22,600 --> 00:10:24,360
I'm itching to point it out for him.

233
00:10:24,520 --> 00:10:25,680
Go on, point it out for him.

234
00:10:26,120 --> 00:10:27,760
Put it here and win, see?

235
00:10:27,880 --> 00:10:30,280
Fill this gap. If she blocks here, he goes there.

236
00:10:31,200 --> 00:10:32,800
Exactly, spot on.

237
00:10:33,360 --> 00:10:34,840
I was going to put it there!

238
00:10:36,800 --> 00:10:37,600
Next!

239
00:10:38,600 --> 00:10:40,720
Bring it on, I'm the defending champ now!

240
00:11:00,640 --> 00:11:01,760
The big gold bowl looks pretty cool too.

241
00:11:03,560 --> 00:11:04,800
Is this that Northeast flavor?

242
00:11:05,440 --> 00:11:05,960
Nope.

243
00:11:06,680 --> 00:11:07,280
It's an upgrade.

244
00:11:16,960 --> 00:11:17,840
This is amazing, Bing!

245
00:11:18,720 --> 00:11:19,360
Good, isn't it?

246
00:11:19,360 --> 00:11:21,520
So good. Absolutely unreal.

247
00:11:28,840 --> 00:11:29,640
Cold noodles.

248
00:11:31,000 --> 00:11:32,400
Whose bowl is this?

249
00:11:32,400 --> 00:11:33,640
You want the small one?

250
00:11:33,640 --> 00:11:34,920
I'd like a small bowl.

251
00:11:34,920 --> 00:11:37,120
I'll make them for everyone. Here's a small bowl.

252
00:11:40,560 --> 00:11:41,520
Aren't you having a bite, Churan?

253
00:11:42,120 --> 00:11:42,840
Be right there!

254
00:11:43,480 --> 00:11:44,080
I'll fix you a small bowl.

255
00:11:52,000 --> 00:11:52,800
Delicious!

256
00:11:53,520 --> 00:11:54,400
Ate it all.

257
00:11:55,160 --> 00:11:56,000
Nothing left to scoop up.

258
00:11:57,080 --> 00:11:58,160
My big bowl...

259
00:11:58,560 --> 00:11:59,920
Not a single noodle left.

260
00:12:06,640 --> 00:12:07,320
Who else hasn't—

261
00:12:07,320 --> 00:12:09,240
Bai hasn't eaten yet. Here.

262
00:12:09,240 --> 00:12:10,680
Give me a bite.

263
00:12:10,680 --> 00:12:11,960
I ate too much rice.

264
00:12:17,000 --> 00:12:17,920
I have... I still have some.

265
00:12:17,920 --> 00:12:18,360
Have some more.

266
00:12:18,360 --> 00:12:20,080
No, I just want some more cilantro.

267
00:12:21,640 --> 00:12:22,520
It smells so good!

268
00:12:22,520 --> 00:12:25,120
Didn't you say you couldn't finish a bowl?

269
00:12:25,600 --> 00:12:27,600
Now you're getting seconds.

270
00:12:28,160 --> 00:12:29,200
Eat some greens.

271
00:12:30,600 --> 00:12:31,400
Sure.

272
00:12:34,880 --> 00:12:36,640
Bing is a great cook.

273
00:12:36,640 --> 00:12:38,840
Even watching him eat noodles looks delicious.

274
00:12:44,480 --> 00:12:45,480
Is there a bed?

275
00:12:47,440 --> 00:12:48,640
I really need to lie down.

276
00:12:48,640 --> 00:12:49,880
I'm so stuffed.

277
00:12:50,040 --> 00:12:51,040
Thanks, Bing.

278
00:12:51,640 --> 00:12:52,320
That hit the spot!

279
00:12:54,000 --> 00:12:54,400
Thanks, man.

280
00:12:58,360 --> 00:12:59,600
Do we need more dishes?

281
00:12:59,840 --> 00:13:00,560
If we had a wok,

282
00:13:00,560 --> 00:13:01,920
in under five minutes,

283
00:13:01,920 --> 00:13:02,840
I could whip up

284
00:13:03,400 --> 00:13:04,640
garlic broccoli for you.

285
00:13:04,840 --> 00:13:06,000
Broccoli?

286
00:13:06,000 --> 00:13:07,320
Just soaking it takes half an hour.

287
00:13:07,680 --> 00:13:08,240
No way.

288
00:13:09,240 --> 00:13:10,880
